na-2026-05-15-1930-corren-las-liebres-62","title":"Corren las liebres","venue":"CCCB Teatre","startsAt":"2026-05-15T19:30:00+02:00","description":"Lorena Ros follows Noa, a Romani trans woman in Barcelona trying to regain custody of her children while facing eviction.","coordinates":[41.383,2.1662],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-15-1930-trillion-63","title":"Trillion","venue":"Phenomena","startsAt":"2026-05-15T19:30:00+02:00","description":"Victor Kossakovsky offers a wordless cinematic interpretation of Sisyphus, continuing the empathy trilogy begun with Gunda.","coordinates":[41.4098,2.1703],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-15-2045-curtmetratges-somni-i-veritat-64","title":"Curtmetratges: Somni i veritat","venue":"CCCB Auditori","startsAt":"2026-05-15T20:45:00+02:00","description":"A short-film program from the official DocsBarcelona calendar around dream and truth.","coordinates":[41.383,2.1662],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-15-2045-plato-3-65","title":"Plato 3","venue":"Cinemes Texas | Sala 1","startsAt":"2026-05-15T20:45:00+02:00","description":"Maria Borrell returns to a closed rural Lleida pub through young people rehearsing a play about nights that still carry old shadows.","coordinates":[41.4024,2.1586],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-15-2045-the-beauty-of-errors-66","title":"The Beauty Of Errors","venue":"Renoir | Sala 6","startsAt":"2026-05-15T20:45:00+02:00","description":"A father-and-son portrait about intimacy, separation, loneliness, and the fear of losing love.","coordinates":[41.3803,2.1609],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-15-2100-do-you-love-me-67","title":"Do You Love Me","venue":"Renoir | Sala 5","startsAt":"2026-05-15T21:00:00+02:00","description":"Lana Daher’s Beirut archive film turns sound, rhythm, and songs into a way of reading collective memory.","coordinates":[41.3803,2.1609],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-1830-amazomania-68","title":"Amazomania","venue":"Renoir | Sala 5","startsAt":"2026-05-16T18:30:00+02:00","description":"Nathan Grossman revisits 1996 footage of the isolated Korubo people, reframing expedition imagery through colonial legacy and territorial conflict.","coordinates":[41.3803,2.1609],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-1830-the-travelers-69","title":"The Travelers","venue":"Casa Montjuic","startsAt":"2026-05-16T18:30:00+02:00","description":"David Bingong follows people waiting at the Morocco-Spain border, keeping hope alive through repeated failed crossings.","coordinates":[41.3717,2.1589],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-1845-80-angry-journalists-70","title":"80 Angry Journalists","venue":"Renoir | Sala 6","startsAt":"2026-05-16T18:45:00+02:00","description":"A contemporary journalism story in the festival line of films that look beyond headlines and put human stakes behind public conflict.","coordinates":[41.3803,2.1609],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-1845-corren-las-liebres-71","title":"Corren las liebres","venue":"Cinemes Texas | Sala 1","startsAt":"2026-05-16T18:45:00+02:00","description":"Lorena Ros follows Noa, a Romani trans woman in Barcelona trying to regain custody of her children while facing eviction.","coordinates":[41.4024,2.1586],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-2000-afterlives-72","title":"Afterlives","venue":"Casa Montjuic","startsAt":"2026-05-16T20:00:00+02:00","description":"Official calendar screening in the DocsBarcelona program.","coordinates":[41.3717,2.1589],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-2030-whispers-in-the-woods-73","title":"Whispers in the Woods","venue":"Renoir | Sala 5","startsAt":"2026-05-16T20:30:00+02:00","description":"Vincent Munier follows forest sounds, wildlife, and family inheritance in a nature documentary built around listening as much as looking.","coordinates":[41.3803,2.1609],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-2045-mailin-74","title":"Mailin","venue":"Renoir | Sala 6","startsAt":"2026-05-16T20:45:00+02:00","description":"Maria Silvia Esteve follows a woman reconstructing memories of abuse by a priest while trying to offer her daughter the childhood she never had.","coordinates":[41.3803,2.1609],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-16-2100-teatres-de-campanya-75","title":"Teatres de Campanya","venue":"CCCB Hall","startsAt":"2026-05-16T21:00:00+02:00","description":"The closing film documents a FiraTarrega urban action with bands, firefighters, buses, and more than 350 participants.","coordinates":[41.383,2.1662],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-17-1800-audience-award-winner-screening-76","title":"Audience award winner screening","venue":"CCCB Teatre","startsAt":"2026-05-17T18:00:00+02:00","description":"Sunday winner-screening slot from the official calendar for the festival audience award.","coordinates":[41.383,2.1662],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"},{"id":"docsbarcelona-2026-05-17-2000-best-film-winner-screening-77","title":"Best film winner screening","venue":"CCCB Teatre","startsAt":"2026-05-17T20:00:00+02:00","description":"Sunday winner-screening slot from the official calendar for the best film winner.","coordinates":[41.383,2.1662],"url":"https://docsbarcelona.com/en/festival/calendar/"}]},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-motogp-fan-fest","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"MotoGP Fan Fest Barcelona","category":"Sports","startsAt":"2026-05-13T12:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-14T22:00:00+02:00","venue":"Placa de Catalunya","neighborhood":"Eixample / City Center","description":"MotoGP''s Barcelona Fan Fest brings the race-weekend atmosphere into Placa de Catalunya before the Grand Prix moves attention north to Montmelo. Expect a public-facing setup with bikes, simulators, games, music, food areas, and rider appearances. It works best as a central-city drop-in plan: easy to combine with Passeig de Gracia, the Gothic Quarter, or an Eixample dinner, but likely to be busy around appearance windows.","url":"https://www.motogp.com","sourceName":"MotoGP / AS","coordinates":[41.3869,2.1701],"price":"Check event site","isGuideWorthy":true,"guideReason":"Connected to a major race weekend and likely to shape city-center crowds.","activations":[{"id":"motogp-simulators","title":"MotoGP simulators and fan zones","venue":"Placa de Catalunya","description":"The public fan-zone layer is the easiest way to feel the race weekend without leaving central Barcelona: simulators, replica bikes, games, food areas, and sponsor activations.","coordinates":[41.3869,2.1701],"url":"https://www.motogp.com"},{"id":"motogp-rider-appearances","title":"Rider appearances","venue":"Placa de Catalunya","description":"Rider appearances are the main reason to time the visit instead of wandering through casually. Expect the biggest crowds around names like Marc Marquez, Alex Marquez, Alex Rins, and Pedro Acosta if confirmed windows hold.","coordinates":[41.3869,2.1701],"url":"https://www.motogp.com"}]},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-catalunya-grand-prix","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"Monster Energy Grand Prix of Catalunya","category":"Sports","startsAt":"2026-05-15T09:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-17T18:00:00+02:00","venue":"Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya","neighborhood":"Montmelo","description":"The Catalunya MotoGP weekend is a major regional sports event rather than a casual city-center activity. The racing happens at Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya in Montmelo, so the practical route is about tickets, train timing, and whether to dedicate a full day outside the city. Even for non-fans, it matters because it can shift hotel demand, transit pressure, and the weekend mood around Barcelona.","url":"https://www.circuitcat.com","sourceName":"Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya / AS","coordinates":[41.57,2.2611],"price":"Ticketed","isGuideWorthy":true,"guideReason":"Major multi-day sports weekend requiring transit and schedule planning."},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-handmade-festival","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"Handmade Festival Barcelona","category":"Markets","startsAt":"2026-05-14T10:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-17T20:00:00+02:00","venue":"Fira Barcelona","neighborhood":"Montjuic","description":"Handmade Festival Barcelona is a creator-led fair built around craft, DIY, materials, demonstrations, workshops, and small-brand discovery. It is a strong fit for travelers who like design markets but want something more hands-on than browsing shops. The Montjuic/Fira setting also makes it easy to pair with museum time, Poble-sec food, or a slower afternoon when the weather makes indoor plans attractive.","url":"https://vamos.barcelona/en/Handmade-Festival-Barcelona-2026--May-14-17/","sourceName":"VAMOS Barcelona","coordinates":[41.3731,2.1513],"price":"Ticketed"},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-museum-night","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"La Nit dels Museus","category":"Culture","startsAt":"2026-05-16T19:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-17T01:00:00+02:00","venue":"Museums across Barcelona","neighborhood":"Citywide","description":"La Nit dels Museus is one of Barcelona''s strongest culture nights: museums and cultural institutions open late, often with free entry, special programming, concerts, workshops, or guided visits. The challenge is not whether there is enough to do; it is choosing a tight route so the night does not become a cross-city queue. Pick one cluster, arrive early, and let the late opening turn the evening into a culture crawl.","url":"https://www.barcelona.cat","sourceName":"Barcelona.cat / Barcelona.com","coordinates":[41.3851,2.1734],"price":"Often free","isGuideWorthy":true,"guideReason":"Citywide one-night event where routing and venue selection matter.","activations":[{"id":"museum-night-macba","title":"Contemporary art route","venue":"MACBA / CCCB area","description":"Use the Raval contemporary-art cluster if you want the night to stay compact: MACBA, CCCB, nearby galleries, and late food or drinks can become one walkable evening.","coordinates":[41.383,2.1662],"url":"https://www.barcelona.cat"},{"id":"museum-night-picasso-born","title":"Old-city museum route","venue":"Picasso Museum / El Born","description":"The Born route works best for visitors who want atmospheric lanes before or after museum time. It pairs naturally with Santa Maria del Mar, wine bars, and dinner nearby.","coordinates":[41.3853,2.1809],"url":"https://www.barcelona.cat"},{"id":"museum-night-montjuic","title":"Montjuic culture route","venue":"Montjuic museums","description":"Montjuic is the best option if you want scale and views, but it needs more routing discipline. Choose one or two institutions instead of bouncing downhill too quickly.","coordinates":[41.3688,2.1536],"url":"https://www.barcelona.cat"}]},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-matsuri","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"Festival Matsuri","category":"Festivals","startsAt":"2026-05-16T11:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-17T21:00:00+02:00","venue":"Moll de la Fusta","neighborhood":"Waterfront / Gothic Quarter","description":"Festival Matsuri turns Moll de la Fusta into a Japanese culture weekend with traditional performance, taiko-style energy, folk dance, workshops, martial arts demonstrations, and food stalls. It is one of the easier festival plans for visitors because the waterfront location sits close to the Gothic Quarter, El Born, and Barceloneta. Use it as a daytime-to-sunset stop, then continue into old-city drinks or seafood nearby.","url":"https://www.barcelona-metropolitan.com/events/matsuri/","sourceName":"Barcelona Metropolitan","coordinates":[41.3799,2.1822],"price":"Check event site"},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-charlotte-dos-santos","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"MASiMAS Festival: Charlotte Dos Santos","category":"Music","startsAt":"2026-05-16T19:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-16T21:00:00+02:00","venue":"Sala Apolo","neighborhood":"Poble-sec","description":"Charlotte Dos Santos'' MASiMAS Festival date gives the week a focused soul and R&B option inside Sala Apolo, one of Barcelona''s most useful music rooms for travelers because the surrounding Poble-sec route is easy. This works as a planned Saturday-night anchor: dinner or vermouth nearby, the show, then Apolo/Poble-sec nightlife if the night still has charge.","url":"https://www.masimas.com","sourceName":"MASiMAS / Barcelona.com","coordinates":[41.3747,2.1695],"price":"Ticketed"},{"id":"barcelona-2026-05-retrobarcelona","cityId":"barcelona","cityName":"Barcelona","title":"RetroBarcelona","category":"Festivals","startsAt":"2026-05-16T10:00:00+02:00","endsAt":"2026-05-17T20:00:00+02:00","venue":"Check event site","neighborhood":"Barcelona","description":"RetroBarcelona is a niche weekend fair for classic games, consoles, collectors, competitions, and talks around retro gaming culture. It is not the broadest Barcelona event of the week, but it is exactly the kind of specific plan that can make a trip feel personal. Best for travelers who would rather spend a few hours with arcade nostalgia, collectors, and playable history than another generic shopping stop.","url":"https://www.barcelona.com/things-to-do-in-barcelona/what-to-do-in-barcelona-in-may","sourceName":"Barcelona.com","coordinates":[41.3851,2.1734],"price":"Check event site"}]}'::jsonb),
